  "generated_text": "To find \\( f(-7) \\), we need to determine which piece of the piecewise function to use. The function \\( f(x) \\) is defined as follows:\n\n\\[\nf(x) =\n\\begin{cases}\n2x + 9 & \\text{if } x < -2, \\\\\n5 - 2x & \\text{if } x \\ge -2.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nStep 1: Identify the correct piece of the function.\nSince \\( -7 < -2 \\), we use the first piece of the function:\n\\[\nf(x) = 2x + 9\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Substitute \\( x = -7 \\) into the first piece of the function.\n\\[\nf(-7) = 2(-7) + 9\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Perform the multiplication.\n\\[\n2(-7) = -14\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Add 9 to the result of the multiplication.\n\\[\n-14 + 9 = -5\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Write the final answer within \\(\\boxed{-5}\\).\n\\[\n\\boxed{-5}\n\\]",
